<pre class=metadata>
Group: test
Shortname: test
Level: 1
Status: LS
ED: http://example.com/foo
Editor: Example Editor
Date: 1970-01-01
Title: Markup in Highlighted Code
Abstract: Verifying that microlighter highlights code containing markup inside, coincident with, and crossing highlight boundaries.
</pre>

<h2 id="inside">Markup Inside Highlight Tokens</h2>

<p>Markup elements (e.g. <code>&lt;span></code>, <code>&lt;mark></code>) nested inside single tokens like keywords, identifiers, and strings:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
func<span>ti</span>on my<span>Func</span>tion() {
    con<mark>st</mark> str = "hel<span>lo</span> world";
}
</pre>

<h2 id="coincident">Markup Coincident with Highlight Tokens</h2>

<p>Markup elements whose boundaries exactly match token boundaries:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
<a href="https://example.com/const">const</a> <dfn export id="myidentifier">myIdentifier</dfn> = <mark>true</mark>;
</pre>

<h2 id="crossing">Markup Crossing Highlight Boundaries</h2>

<p>Markup elements spanning across multiple tokens or starting/ending mid-token:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
<a href="https://example.com/test">let a =</a> 1;
foo<mark>bar + baz</mark>qux();
/* A comment with <em>markup crossing</em> the comment */
</pre>
